Source: epistle
Section: mail
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Glyndor <packages@glyndor.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
# Cargo and rustc are deliberately absent. debian/rules builds for a musl
# target, and Debian's toolchain ships no musl standard library, so the build
# needs a rustup toolchain the workflow installs and pins to the same version
# rust-ci.yml uses. Declaring Debian's rustc here would make dpkg-checkbuilddeps
# pass on a compiler that is not the one doing the work - which is the defect
# Glyndor/epistle#716 is about, stated as a dependency.
#
# The cost, so it is a decision rather than a side effect: `dpkg-buildpackage`
# on a plain Debian box no longer works from Build-Depends alone; the musl
# target has to be present first. That is acceptable here because the releases
# standard rules out submitting to the Debian archive - this package is built
# by one workflow, for one self-hosted archive.
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
